findings.body:
The React Scan loader logs import failures with `console.error`, but the TanStack loader swallows them silently. A broken `./devtools` chunk in development would render nothing and leave no trace in the console.

::code{file="web/app/components/devtools/tanstack/loader.tsx" lines="6-12"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Pick one behavior and apply it to both loaders. Logging matches the React Scan loader, and a shared helper would keep them from drifting.

The React Scan loader renders a visible `Loading devtools...` text node as its Suspense fallback. The TanStack loader uses `fallback={null}`. Because the React Scan component returns null, that text shows in the layout body until the chunk loads, and that is the only visible effect of the loader. Dev-only UI text in the layout is probably unintended here.

::code{file="web/app/components/devtools/react-scan/loader.tsx" lines="19-23"}

Use `fallback={null}` as the TanStack loader does, unless the text was added on purpose.

The description says `web/app/components/devtools/index.ts` was simplified into clean barrel exports. That file does not exist at head, and the diff does not add or change it. Nothing imports a barrel now, so the description is inaccurate or the change was dropped. Reviewers may look for an export surface that is not there.

::diff{file="web/app/components/devtools/tanstack/loader.tsx" lines="1-6"}

Update the description, or add the barrel if it is still wanted.

The TanStack devtools loader is now rendered before `{children}`, but before this PR the devtools were rendered after them. This only changes the order of siblings in the React tree. The TanStack panel is a floating overlay, so the visible result is probably unchanged. Still, the order change is undocumented, and a devtools component that depends on mount order could behave differently.

::diff{file="web/context/query-client.tsx" lines="18-24"}

This is probably fine. Confirm it is intentional, or move the loader after `children` to match the old order.

The base code statically imported `ReactScan` into `layout.tsx`, which pulled the `react-scan` package into the main bundle. The new `ReactScanLoader` returns null when `IS_DEV` is false, before the lazy child is rendered, so `import('./scan')` never runs in production. The dynamic import also gives the devtools a separate chunk in development.

::diff{file="web/app/components/devtools/react-scan/loader.tsx" lines="1-17"}

This is the core of the change, and the gating is correct.
